======================================================================================================================
  O1  [MODEL-INDEPENDENT] The SN-Ia host-mass step at the a0 scale
        standing: a real step of -0.050 +- 0.007 mag (6.9 sigma) sits where g_bar crosses a0 (log M* 9.6-10.2 vs the step at 10); the decisive fixed-mass test finds acceleration adds nothing beyond mass (partial +0.030 vs mass -0.170) but has only 18% (23% alt) power against the framework's own step model
        keep:     keep the step (-0.050 +- 0.007 mag at log M* ~ 10); any construction that ties it to a0 must predict a fixed-mass acceleration dependence, which the present sample cannot see (80% power needs a 0.142 mag step)
  O2  [MODEL-INDEPENDENT] The environmental null: a0 tracks rho_Lambda, not the local density (the BIG-SPARC pipeline)
        standing: the rho_local fork (d log a0/d log rho_env = +1/2) is excluded at 13-34 sigma on 175 SPARC; no committed .out (the number is the committed ledger EMPIRICAL_TESTS.md A14)
        keep:     a0 must not depend on the ambient density (|d log a0/d log rho_env| << 1/2); the source is the cosmic rho_Lambda
  O3  [SOFT             ] The measured kappa
        standing: kappa = 1/2 is FITTED and sits 0.46 sigma from the BTFR value and 0.29 sigma from the distance-free one; the two estimators share galaxies (not independent); 1/2 vs 1/(2 pi): Delta chi^2 63.9 vs 154.3 (~2.2 sigma, forecast-grade)
        keep:     any construction that ties kappa must land inside 0.465 +- 0.076 (BTFR) and 0.55 +- 0.17 (distance-free); the record carries kappa = 1/2 as fitted
  O4  [CONTESTED        ] Flat a0(z): the z ~ 2.5 deep-MOND BTFR zero point and the MUSE confrontation
        standing: the registered test cannot run (0 of 2 deep-MOND rotators); the on-disk proxy (+0.636 +- 0.054 dex) is at high acceleration and is NOT the registered test; the framework predicts 0.00 against LCDM-native +0.33 dex
        keep:     a0(z) flat to < 1% for z <= 5 on a true Lambda (the distinctive prediction); the decisive test needs 3 deep-MOND rotators at +-0.10 dex or 4 at +-0.20 dex at z ~ 2.5
  O5  [SOFT             ] The Oort-cloud comet anisotropy as an external-field instrument (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21966646)
        standing: spike quadrupole -0.0268 +- 0.0389 (0.7 sigma) against a predicted A ~ 0.12: UNDERPOWERED (N ~ 3197 needed), recorded as such, not as a null; the nu0-correlated pair with DR4 collapses to 16.7%, indistinguishable from constant-a0 17%, once stage76's nu0 bound applies
        keep:     no constraint yet; a prospective instrument that needs original 1/a and ~3000 spike comets
  O6  [CONTESTED        ] The directional external-field test (rotation-curve asymmetry toward the external field)
        standing: an exploratory ~2-sigma-at-best hint that did not reproduce; the AQUAL floor signal registers at only ~0.3 sigma in the n = 16 stack; 'pure MI predicts exactly zero' was retracted (the derived dipole is 4.2-22.3%)
        keep:     no constraint yet (consistent with zero); a construction's predicted dipole (4-22% for the MI class) needs ~1400-6000 galaxies
  O7  [SOFT             ] The Milky Way's local vertical force
        standing: full AQUAL on McMillan-2017 baryons matches the vertical force at +0.2 sigma (Eilers slope +1.2 sigma) but only with ~30% more stellar mass for v_c; Route A's joint box clears at 1.502 sigma (p = 0.03, a minimax criterion) and its floor Sigma_dyn(1.1 kpc) 78.5/82.7 exceeds Bovy & Rix's 68 +- 4
        keep:     Sigma_dyn(|z| < 1.1 kpc) = 68-74 (+-4-6) Msun/pc^2 at R0 with census-compatible baryons, jointly with v_c(R0)
  O8  [SOFT             ] The Lyman-alpha forest b-cutoff sign
        standing: the framework's b sits above the measured b0 in every bin (the sign is robust) at 1.1-9.0 sigma on the statistical channel but only 0.4-0.9 sigma on the calibration channel; the magnitude is convention-owned (a factor ~32)
        keep:     the b0 cutoff sign (framework b above b0) must not grow beyond the calibration channel's 0.4-0.9 sigma in a construction's forest-gas acceleration
